[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue: "dates parse month first". The reports under it
describe two different problems. The queued fix covers one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. When the parser fix ships, #4471 will close and the other problem will still have
reports and no ticket.
</Callout>

## What the reports show

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

Counts come from the reports and the tenant directory at render time. A report belongs to a problem
by its tenant (locale and booking form), never by its subject line, its intake tag or how the reporter
describes it.

## The two problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first.** A day-first tenant's dates come out with day
and month swapped. This is the bug #4471 describes. Reports come in by app, email and form.

**`hint`: the booking form teaches the wrong order.** Booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date
field, so people at a day-first tenant type the month first, and the form reads it their way. Only
form reports from booking-v3 tenants belong here. Fixing the parser does not touch this: the fix is
the hint text or the form.

A few reports describe a date that is one day off instead of a month flip. The desk filed them by
tenant, under `parser`, and footnotes them. They are counted once, in that row.

## Why the merge hid this

- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on the subject line. The same subjects
  ("Wrong day on the invite", "Appointment moved by itself") come in for both problems.
- Intake tags a report from the reporter's browser, before anyone looks at the tenant. The "tagged
  wrong" column shows how often that guess names the other problem.
- The ticket export comes in pages that overlap, so the same report can arrive twice. One id is one
  report.

## What to do

- Keep one ticket per problem, each with the count shown above.
- Decide a new matching rule: group by cause (tenant locale and booking form), not by subject. Write
  it as a new decision record that replaces 0001. Do not edit 0001.
- Count reports by id before you quote a number.

